    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d67">

                <pb facs="0146" n="980" xml:id="pg980"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 600.119/613</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-08T19:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 8, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7180. For Sheldon [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>307. Your No. 365. Embassy No. 9311, April 2, 9 p.m. We approve of the statement
                    of the functions of local trade committee in northern European capitals as set
                    out in Foreign Office communication which you quote. Our ministers at these
                    capitals are being notified of this approval.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
